Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T04:54:53-08:00","id":345679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/339545-your-pack-encounters?p=345554#post345554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know who Cole is by I'll take it from the rest of the guys that he's either a spirit of a Ridden. if he's a Ridden then its death at the instant for him and if he's a spirit we'll either make him into a fetish or hunt him back into the Shadow and teach him a lesson, or five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cole is a Spirit of Compassion who somehow found a way to take on human form without possessing anything. He has the power to render himself completely unnoticeable, or to make people forget he ever existed, kind of like Lunacy. Cole uses his powers to help people deal with emotional trauma, and then removes the memory of their meeting so that whatever he said to them will seem like it was their own thoughts, and thus allow them to heal properly.<br /> <br /> When it comes to emotional torment, he's quite good at healing that. He's... less adept when it comes to physical pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thank